---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { cities, cityLabel, destinationNames } from "../data/cities";
import { cityPath, money, monthlyCostFor } from "../lib/seo";

const title = "Digital Nomad Cost of Living Comparison | NomadBurn";
const description =
  "Compare rough 2026 rent and living-cost estimates for digital nomad cities, then see how each destination changes monthly burn and savings runway.";
const exampleCity = "Chiang Mai";
const example = cities[exampleCity];
const exampleTotal = monthlyCostFor(exampleCity);
const exampleWorkspace = exampleTotal - example.baseLivingCost - example.colivingRent - 100 - 150;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/digital-nomad-cost-of-living/">
  <section class="content-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">City comparison</p>
    <h1>Digital nomad cost of living comparison</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Compare rough monthly planning assumptions for popular remote-work cities, including expanded
      Eastern Europe and Central Europe coverage, then use the burn rate calculator to replace the
      defaults with your own income and savings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-panel">
    <h2>2026 Planning Estimates, Not Live Quotes</h2>
    <p>
      Compare {destinationNames.length} city planning baselines in USD per month for one person.
      The accommodation columns are alternatives: the sample total includes coliving only,
      plus base living costs, three coworking or cafe work sessions per week, $100 in fixed
      costs, and a $150 monthly travel or visa buffer.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>City</th>
            <th>Base living</th>
            <th>Coliving</th>
            <th>Airbnb solo</th>
            <th>Hostel</th>
            <th>Sample monthly setup</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            destinationNames.map((city) => (
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <a href={cityPath(city)}>{cityLabel(city)}</a>
                  <br />
                  <a href={`/?${new URLSearchParams({ destination: city, lifestyle: "comfortable" })}#burn-form`}>Plan this city</a>
                </td>
                <td>{money(cities[city].baseLivingCost)}</td>
                <td>{money(cities[city].colivingRent)}</td>
                <td>{money(cities[city].airbnbRent)}</td>
                <td>{money(cities[city].hostelRent)}</td>
                <td>{money(monthlyCostFor(city))}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">
      Last reviewed: July 2026. Sample setup assumes coliving, three coworking or cafe work
      sessions per week, $100 fixed costs, and a $150 flight or visa buffer. Rent, coworking,
      SIM/data, and seasonal travel can move quickly. See the
      <a href="/methodology/">NomadBurn cost methodology</a> before treating any estimate as a real
      quote.
    </p>
    <p>
      “Plan this city” opens the calculator with that city and coliving selected. Review its
      example savings, income, and other defaults before using the result for your own plan.
      Comparing against a spending limit? See the
      <a href="/best-digital-nomad-cities-under-2000/">city planning baselines under $2,000 a month</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-panel">
    <h2>How the sample monthly total is calculated</h2>
    <p>
      Base living costs + one accommodation option + monthly coworking or cafe work costs
      + fixed costs + travel or visa buffer. Base living is a combined planning assumption,
      not a set of individually verified local prices.
    </p>
    <div class="formula-box">
      <strong>{cityLabel(exampleCity)}: coliving example</strong>
      <span>
        {money(example.baseLivingCost)} base living + {money(example.colivingRent)} coliving
        + {money(exampleWorkspace)} workspace + $100 fixed costs + $150 travel or visa buffer
        = {money(exampleTotal)} per month.
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">
      The workspace estimate uses three visits per week across 4.33 weeks. Displayed amounts
      are rounded to whole dollars. This example uses the same July 2026 planning assumptions
      as the table; it is not a current market quote. Check one-time relocation costs, housing
      deposits, and personal expenses separately, and replace assumptions with your own quotes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-panel">
    <h2>Cost of living is not burn rate</h2>
    <p>
      Cost of living tells you what a city might cost before income enters the picture. Burn rate is
      the part of that cost your net monthly income still does not cover. If you need the monthly
      gap itself, use the <a href="/digital-nomad-burn-rate-calculator/">burn rate guide and calculator</a>.
      If the city is still undecided, stay here and compare destinations first.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
